   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Split the integral at any constant k in the domain of the integrand: \\( g(x) = \\int_{k}^{2 x} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} \\, dt - \\int_{k}^{x} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} \\, dt \\), and apply the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus to each piece.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            2,
            "ExponentialE"
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "With the chain rule, \\( g'(x) = f\\left(2 x\\right) \\cdot 2 - f\\left(x\\right) \\cdot 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": 2
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At \\( x = e \\): the limits are \\( 2 e \\) and \\( e \\), with derivatives \\( 2 \\) and \\( 1 \\), and \\( f\\left(2 e\\right) = \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 1 \\), \\( f\\left(e\\right) = 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Ln",
               2
            ],
            1
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So \\( g'\\left(e\\right) = \\left(\\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} + 1\\right) \\cdot 2 - 1 \\cdot 1 = 1 + 2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
